                                        "sense_id": "617d6fba-75ed-3310-b3fd-bc63342cc032",
                                        "entry_id": "b9646c3c-1982-3442-aaad-fdd63143a009",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of, relating to, or appropriate to a villain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c9448096-c8a5-3997-acf5-903a0161f6d1",
                                        "entry_id": "b9646c3c-1982-3442-aaad-fdd63143a009",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Wicked, offensive, or reprehensible in nature or behaviour; nefarious."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7384014e-f699-4dee-a848-e9faf8540394",
                                                "sense_id": "c9448096-c8a5-3997-acf5-903a0161f6d1",
                                                "text": "Tuc[ca]. […] Can thy Author doe it impudently enough? / Hiſt[rio]. O, I warrant you, Captaine: and ſpitefully inough too; he ha's one of the moſt ouerflowing villanous wits, in Rome. He will ſlander any man that breathes; If he diſguſt him. / Tucca. I'le know the poor, egregious, nitty Raſcall; and he haue ſuch commendable Qualities, I'le cheriſh him: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb3d526f-5587-44bf-9bf6-fe4f2db9d10d",
                                                "sense_id": "c9448096-c8a5-3997-acf5-903a0161f6d1",
                                                "text": "Bah! to this toilet for the villainous boredom of church."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
